Grammar

    0 $accept: decl $end

    1 decl: type list ';'

    2 type: INT

    3 list: list ',' ID
    4     | ID


Terminals, with rules where they appear

    $end (0) 0
    ',' (44) 3
    ';' (59) 1
    error (256)
    INT (258) 2
    ID (259) 3 4


Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

    $accept (7)
        on left: 0
    decl (8)
        on left: 1
        on right: 0
    type (9)
        on left: 2
        on right: 1
    list (10)
        on left: 3 4
        on right: 1 3


State 0

    0 $accept: • decl $end

    INT  shift, and go to state 1

    decl  go to state 2
    type  go to state 3


State 1

    2 type: INT •

    $default  reduce using rule 2 (type)


State 2

    0 $accept: decl • $end

    $end  shift, and go to state 4


State 3

    1 decl: type • list ';'

    ID  shift, and go to state 5

    list  go to state 6


State 4

    0 $accept: decl $end •

    $default  accept


State 5

    4 list: ID •

    $default  reduce using rule 4 (list)


State 6

    1 decl: type list • ';'
    3 list: list • ',' ID

    ';'  shift, and go to state 7
    ','  shift, and go to state 8


State 7

    1 decl: type list ';' •

    $default  reduce using rule 1 (decl)


State 8

    3 list: list ',' • ID

    ID  shift, and go to state 9


State 9

    3 list: list ',' ID •

    $default  reduce using rule 3 (list)
